/Creator ( )
/Producer ( )
/Author (Fahlman, Scott E.;Lebiere, Christian)
/Keywords (*ALGORITHMS;*NEURAL NETS;*COMPUTER NETWORKS;*COMPUTER ARCHITECTURE;INPUT;DETECTORS;NETWORKS;CORRELATION;SIGNALS;LEARNING;ARCHITECTURE;ERRORS;TOPOLOGY;STRUCTURES;LAYERS;TRAINING;OUTPUT;PROPAGATION)
/Subject (Cascade-Correlation is a new architecture and supervised learning algorithm for artificial neural networks. Instead of just adjusting the weights in a network of fixed topology, Cascade-Correlation begins with a minimal network, then automatically trains and adds new hidden units one by one, creating a multi-layer structure. Once a new hidden unit has been added to the network, its input-side weights are frozen. This unit then becomes a permanent feature-detector in the network, available for producing outputs or for creating other, more complex feature detectors. The Cascade-Correlation architecture has several advantages over existing algorithms it learns very quickly, the network determines its own size and topology, it retains the structures it has built even if the training set changes, and it requires no back-propagation of error signals through the connections of the network.)
/Title (The Cascade-Correlation Learning Architecture)
/Filename (/pdf/TR/ADA256635.pdf)
>>
